WEBVTT

00:02.752 --> 00:04.963
In other words, 2 here is the coefficient.

00:05.046 --> 00:08.174
To express an algebraic expression,
you combine like terms.

00:08.258 --> 00:09.592
So, in this equation...

00:09.676 --> 00:11.386
Uh...

00:12.095 --> 00:13.346
Huh?

00:14.723 --> 00:15.932
What?

01:46.022 --> 01:49.943
SATURDAY, APRIL 25th

01:50.735 --> 01:51.569
Huh?

01:52.320 --> 01:54.864
There's something in class
you don't understand?

01:54.948 --> 01:57.867
Even going back over everything
we've covered so far didn't help.

01:57.951 --> 02:00.787
So, that's why you were
acting all weird in class!

02:01.830 --> 02:02.664
By the way...

02:03.456 --> 02:04.958
how are you at math?

02:05.041 --> 02:06.292
I suck at it!

02:06.376 --> 02:07.877
Yeah, figures.

02:07.961 --> 02:09.629
Ah! In that case...

02:10.964 --> 02:12.841
Huh? Studying?

02:14.759 --> 02:18.304
So, when stuff like X and Y starts
showing up, you get all mixed up.

02:18.388 --> 02:20.682
Please, Eri! Teach me!

02:21.266 --> 02:22.559
No way!

02:22.642 --> 02:24.644
I'm juggling work and housework as it is,

02:24.727 --> 02:28.064
and I'm also trying to figure out
how to turn you back to normal.

02:28.148 --> 02:30.150
I can't argue with that...

02:30.900 --> 02:32.944
But please, help me out here!

02:33.027 --> 02:36.072
It's not like he's actually dumb.

02:36.739 --> 02:38.992
Go ask your teacher.

02:39.075 --> 02:41.035
That's what school is for, right?

02:41.119 --> 02:42.370
It's just...

02:42.453 --> 02:46.166
the teacher's a little younger than me,
so it's kind of hard to ask.

02:46.749 --> 02:47.917
What?!

02:48.001 --> 02:51.796
Either drop that pointless pride,
or deal with it yourself!

02:54.591 --> 02:56.301
She hung up on me.

02:56.384 --> 02:58.803
LIBRARY

02:59.721 --> 03:00.722
No good.

03:00.805 --> 03:01.723
I don't get it!

03:01.806 --> 03:03.141
If I don't figure it out,

03:03.224 --> 03:05.894
I'll never understand
what comes up in later lessons!

03:05.977 --> 03:09.522
At this rate, I'm just gonna keep
falling further and further behind!

03:10.398 --> 03:12.442
What am I supposed to do?

03:12.525 --> 03:14.444
Are you looking something up?

03:17.071 --> 03:19.574
You're Ogami, right?

03:20.783 --> 03:22.827
I've seen him in my class.

03:22.911 --> 03:24.954
Uh, let's see... Shira... ishi...

03:25.538 --> 03:27.749
Yep, Ryo Shiraishi!

03:28.833 --> 03:30.376
Okay, I see.

03:30.460 --> 03:33.171
This is probably a problem
that goes back even earlier.

03:33.254 --> 03:34.297
Huh?

03:34.380 --> 03:37.175
Maybe you never got the hang of
math in elementary school,

03:37.258 --> 03:40.178
so now it's all getting mixed together
and confusing you.

03:41.846 --> 03:44.432
Come to think of it,
all I did was fool around.

03:45.141 --> 03:46.267
I know!

03:46.351 --> 03:48.686
I come here to study pretty often, too!

03:48.770 --> 03:49.896
Let's do it together!

03:49.979 --> 03:50.897
Huh?

03:50.980 --> 03:52.982
MODERN MIDDLE SCHOOL
MATH 1

04:03.493 --> 04:05.203
MATH QUIZ

04:06.037 --> 04:07.997
QUIZ
JUZO OGAMI

04:12.001 --> 04:14.420
I got a perfect score on the quiz
because of you!

04:14.504 --> 04:15.630
Thanks!

04:15.713 --> 04:19.926
No, it's because you worked hard
and relearned the basics, Ogami.

04:20.635 --> 04:23.179
Damn, I'm so freaking happy!

04:26.599 --> 04:28.393
Seriously, thank you so much...

04:28.476 --> 04:29.727
Master!

04:29.811 --> 04:31.479
Huh? What's with "Master"?

04:32.146 --> 04:34.274
I can never thank you enough!

04:34.899 --> 04:37.568
But first, let me buy you a drink.

04:37.652 --> 04:40.530
Why do you suddenly sound like an old man?

04:44.409 --> 04:45.702
How about over there?

04:52.000 --> 04:53.209
Sorry!

04:53.293 --> 04:55.753
Watch where you're going, brat.

04:56.379 --> 04:58.506
Let's go.
There's an open table over there.

04:58.589 --> 05:00.341
Cocky little brats.

05:01.217 --> 05:03.594
Wasting their parents' money.

05:03.678 --> 05:06.055
Punks think the world's a joke.

05:06.681 --> 05:09.309
No, but seriously, it's amazing!

05:09.392 --> 05:11.185
While teaching me every day,

05:11.269 --> 05:13.646
you were studying even more yourself.

05:13.730 --> 05:15.189
Rather than being diligent,

05:15.773 --> 05:18.818
it feels like you've got
some kind of goal you're aiming for!

05:21.237 --> 05:23.573
Don't tell anyone else in class, okay?

05:24.365 --> 05:25.658
The truth is...

05:25.742 --> 05:27.327
I want to become a doctor.

05:27.410 --> 05:28.328
That's incredible!

05:28.911 --> 05:30.955
What's the difference if people know?

05:31.039 --> 05:33.333
Well, it's just kind of embarrassing.

05:34.292 --> 05:37.211
When I was little,
my mom died of an illness.

05:37.962 --> 05:41.966
And on days when my dad wasn't around,
my grandma took care of me.

05:42.633 --> 05:46.679
But lately, my grandma's health
has gotten worse.

05:47.430 --> 05:48.473
So, I decided.

05:49.057 --> 05:53.853
I want people like my mom and grandma
to live longer.

05:53.936 --> 05:57.065
So, I thought I'd become a doctor.

05:57.982 --> 05:59.442
That's all.

06:00.777 --> 06:01.903
Grandmaster!

06:01.986 --> 06:04.947
I got promoted again?
Please, stop with that!

06:05.031 --> 06:06.407
I'm touched!

06:07.116 --> 06:08.785
I'm nowhere near that!

06:08.868 --> 06:10.620
What brought this on?

06:12.830 --> 06:13.998
No, honestly...

06:14.499 --> 06:16.042
I really meant that.

06:16.709 --> 06:18.795
I say I'm bad with kids...

06:19.462 --> 06:21.798
but maybe that's because

06:21.881 --> 06:24.509
I've never really treated them
as individual people.

06:25.426 --> 06:26.803
At the very least,

06:27.428 --> 06:29.680
he's way more admirable than I am.

06:33.976 --> 06:35.770
I heard you two talking.

06:36.354 --> 06:40.066
Aiming to be a doctor these days?
Aside from being a waste of money,

06:40.149 --> 06:42.944
it just makes me wonder
if you're plain stupid!

06:43.027 --> 06:44.112
What?

06:44.195 --> 06:47.573
What you're saying
is so out of touch with reality.

06:47.657 --> 06:49.700
You really oughta look at the data more.

06:50.284 --> 06:52.620
Maybe I should just punch him.

06:52.703 --> 06:54.705
No, you shouldn't get violent!

06:54.789 --> 06:57.125
And you, too, Glasses...

06:57.208 --> 06:59.877
Struggling with homework
in your first year of middle school?

06:59.961 --> 07:03.172
That's just dumb, honestly!

07:03.256 --> 07:06.968
And then trying your ass off
when you're clearly not cut out for it?

07:07.051 --> 07:09.470
Shows just how stupid you are.

07:09.554 --> 07:11.055
I mean, being dumb is--

07:11.139 --> 07:14.016
Thanks for the advice.

07:14.100 --> 07:16.018
But we've had enough.

07:16.102 --> 07:16.936
Wha...

07:17.019 --> 07:18.980
I'm saying this for your sake!

07:19.063 --> 07:23.651
What you're saying has nothing to do
with why I want to become a doctor.

07:23.734 --> 07:26.404
More than that,
even if you were technically right,

07:26.487 --> 07:29.615
calling others "idiots"
for not accepting that,

07:29.699 --> 07:31.534
is just wrong of you as a person.

07:32.118 --> 07:35.913
And I don't want someone like that
laughing at my friend's hard work!

07:38.416 --> 07:39.667
Listen--

07:39.750 --> 07:40.918
That's enough.

07:41.002 --> 07:43.004
You're being loud.

07:43.087 --> 07:46.382
That's exactly what you call
"none of your damn business."

07:46.466 --> 07:47.550
Gross.

07:47.633 --> 07:49.135
He's getting destroyed.

07:49.218 --> 07:51.637
Anyway, what do you do for a living?

07:52.722 --> 07:54.348
All of you go to hell!

07:59.187 --> 08:00.855
So you speak up when it counts!

08:00.938 --> 08:02.690
I've found new respect for you.

08:02.773 --> 08:04.775
I just kind of lost my temper.

08:05.359 --> 08:07.278
That really wasn't good, was it?

08:07.361 --> 08:08.279
It was awesome!

08:10.656 --> 08:12.492
Goddamn kids!

08:12.575 --> 08:14.702
Make a fool outta me?

08:14.785 --> 08:16.287
As I pass by,

08:16.370 --> 08:18.414
I'll nail 'em with my killer kick!

08:18.498 --> 08:20.625
And send 'em splashing into the river!

08:20.708 --> 08:23.085
I bet he's thinking crap like that.

08:23.794 --> 08:24.962
Good grief.

08:26.380 --> 08:27.548
Boss!

08:27.632 --> 08:28.966
Yeah, I know.

08:29.050 --> 08:30.885
I'm just gonna teach him a little lesson.

08:31.969 --> 08:34.680
That's going a little too far, sonny.

08:40.853 --> 08:42.897
Go cool down a bit.

08:42.980 --> 08:48.152
- Then learn a thing or two from my master.
- What?

08:48.236 --> 08:49.195
Oops.

08:49.278 --> 08:50.279
Here.

08:50.363 --> 08:51.614
You forgot something.

08:52.406 --> 08:54.784
Your precious laptop.

08:54.867 --> 08:56.786
Mind your own damn business!

08:59.080 --> 08:59.956
Huh?

09:00.039 --> 09:01.666
Did something just fall in?

09:01.749 --> 09:02.833
Who knows?

09:07.004 --> 09:10.341
She may not look it,
but she gets lonely easily.

09:16.222 --> 09:17.181
Kozu--

09:28.859 --> 09:29.944
It's me.

09:43.124 --> 09:44.542
Mornin'!

09:45.376 --> 09:47.920
This place is a total dump, Boss!

09:51.716 --> 09:54.093
The living room's filthy, too!

09:54.176 --> 09:57.013
I haven't called
the housekeeper in a while.

09:57.096 --> 09:59.640
Then just clean it yourself!

09:59.724 --> 10:02.226
No can do. I've never done that before.

10:02.310 --> 10:05.062
Besides, men don't do
that kind of stuff, you know.

10:07.064 --> 10:08.149
Boss...

10:08.232 --> 10:10.818
- That's not funny.
- Huh?

10:10.901 --> 10:13.863
What year do you think this is?

10:13.946 --> 10:17.199
Seriously, update your values already!

10:18.326 --> 10:20.077
Keep that in mind, okay?

10:20.161 --> 10:21.329
Yeah, yeah, I got it.

10:21.912 --> 10:24.290
Who wants to join our club?

10:24.373 --> 10:25.916
Oh, club activities, huh?

10:26.000 --> 10:26.834
TENNIS CLUB

10:26.917 --> 10:29.128
They did say
clubs were starting up this week.

10:29.712 --> 10:31.339
Have you decided what club you're joining?

10:31.422 --> 10:32.757
Hmm...

10:32.840 --> 10:34.925
I'm gonna pass on the athletic clubs.

10:35.009 --> 10:37.053
Huh? Why's that?

10:37.637 --> 10:38.804
Hey!

10:38.888 --> 10:41.098
Sorry! Throw it back over here!

10:49.732 --> 10:50.941
You okay?

10:51.025 --> 10:53.903
I'd stand out way too much in this world.

10:54.737 --> 10:55.905
Oh, what club?

10:55.988 --> 10:58.157
I'm thinking maybe kendo.

10:58.240 --> 10:59.283
Huh?

11:00.534 --> 11:02.828
I actually did it a little before.

11:02.912 --> 11:07.416
I just like it, and I want to do my best
balancing it with my studies, too.

11:07.500 --> 11:08.918
Master!

11:09.460 --> 11:10.461
What about you, Ogami?

11:10.544 --> 11:14.131
Oh, I figured I should probably avoid
athletic clubs.

11:14.215 --> 11:16.592
Then maybe a cultural club?

11:16.675 --> 11:18.469
Looks like there are all kinds.

11:20.763 --> 11:21.597
Huh?

11:22.181 --> 11:23.974
Home Ec Club?

11:24.058 --> 11:27.311
Cooking, sewing,
and even laundry and cleaning, too.

11:27.895 --> 11:30.106
It's probably all girls anyway, right?

11:30.189 --> 11:31.524
For real, Boss? Again?

11:31.607 --> 11:33.067
Hmm? Hey...

11:33.150 --> 11:36.320
I can't just let that one slide, Ogami.

11:37.738 --> 11:39.198
- Sis!
- Huh?

11:39.281 --> 11:41.742
You're Master's big sis?

11:41.826 --> 11:46.038
Yep. And I'm the president of the
Home Ec Club you were just talking about.

11:46.122 --> 11:49.041
My little brother's told me about you.

11:49.125 --> 11:53.379
Still, what are you, a newly arrived
time traveler or something?

11:53.963 --> 11:56.882
Sure, there are all kinds of differences
between men and women.

11:56.966 --> 11:59.051
But that's beside the point.

11:59.135 --> 12:03.222
If you're alive, you eat, so you cook.

12:03.305 --> 12:06.851
You make trash, so you clean it up.
That's why...

12:06.934 --> 12:10.855
you should learn to wipe your own butt.

12:10.938 --> 12:13.065
That's all there is to it.

12:14.984 --> 12:17.611
"Wipe your own butt"!

12:17.695 --> 12:18.571
I see!

12:18.654 --> 12:20.614
Phrased like that, you get it, huh?

12:21.198 --> 12:24.118
Once you learn how to do it,
you can let someone else take over.

12:24.201 --> 12:27.371
Knowing the effort it takes
makes you appreciate it properly.

12:27.455 --> 12:28.372
All right!

12:29.248 --> 12:31.500
There's a trial session today, so come by!

12:31.584 --> 12:32.334
Huh?

12:32.418 --> 12:34.545
Rather, I'd better see you there!

12:34.628 --> 12:36.046
No, I...

12:37.339 --> 12:40.050
If you don't come,
I'm not letting you borrow Ryo anymore.

12:40.134 --> 12:42.261
No way! Don't take my Master!

12:42.344 --> 12:45.389
To think she'd threaten
a legendary assassin...

12:45.473 --> 12:46.974
HOME EC ROOM

12:47.558 --> 12:49.768
Okay, since this is just a trial session,

12:49.852 --> 12:54.023
let's keep it simple today
and make rice balls and miso soup!

12:54.106 --> 12:55.357
Okay!

12:55.441 --> 12:57.818
There are actually
quite a few guys here, too.

12:57.902 --> 12:58.903
Now then...

12:58.986 --> 13:02.198
since we've got the venue,
how about a little contest?

13:02.281 --> 13:03.115
Huh?

13:03.699 --> 13:05.910
If it turns out to be boring, you win.

13:05.993 --> 13:09.079
Then, as part of club activities,
I'll help out with your chores

13:09.163 --> 13:11.165
for the next six months.

13:11.248 --> 13:12.041
Huh?

13:12.124 --> 13:14.668
She's pretty damn confrontational.

13:15.336 --> 13:16.545
And if I lose?

13:18.214 --> 13:19.256
You join!

13:19.340 --> 13:21.550
No complaints if you had fun, right?

13:45.199 --> 13:46.450
Damn, that's good.

13:46.951 --> 13:48.452
FEEL FREE TO TAKE LEFTOVERS HOME!

13:48.536 --> 13:50.621
You can take home whatever's left over!

13:50.704 --> 13:54.083
If you had a good time,
we'd love to have you join the club!

13:55.793 --> 13:57.628
So, what did you think?

13:57.711 --> 13:58.837
Uh...

13:59.672 --> 14:01.674
How can I put it? It was...

14:01.757 --> 14:02.800
just okay.

14:02.883 --> 14:04.093
Huh? Boss?

14:06.887 --> 14:08.138
I see!

14:08.222 --> 14:09.306
Well, too bad!

14:09.390 --> 14:12.726
No, I mean, it's not like it was boring,

14:12.810 --> 14:14.520
so let's call it a draw.

14:14.603 --> 14:15.646
Nah!

14:15.729 --> 14:17.398
The contest isn't over yet.

14:17.481 --> 14:18.357
Huh?

14:18.899 --> 14:20.150
See...

14:22.486 --> 14:23.988
I mean, that was petty!

14:24.780 --> 14:26.949
Just because you don't wanna lose!

14:27.032 --> 14:27.867
Huh?

14:27.950 --> 14:31.412
You were going, "This is damn good!"
about the miso soup, weren't you?

14:31.495 --> 14:32.997
No, that's not it!

14:33.080 --> 14:34.540
It was good, sure.

14:34.623 --> 14:37.710
It was good, but I was kinda like,
"Okay, that's enough."

14:37.793 --> 14:38.627
Really?

14:39.628 --> 14:44.091
Honestly, it just didn't move me enough
to make me want to join the club.

14:44.884 --> 14:46.594
You want the leftovers I made?

14:46.677 --> 14:49.054
Huh? Really? Sweet!

14:49.555 --> 14:50.598
No.

14:50.681 --> 14:52.057
Actually, I'm good.

14:52.141 --> 14:53.142
Why?

14:53.225 --> 14:56.687
More importantly, you're heading
to the lab for your checkup, right?

15:01.942 --> 15:03.694
MIDDLE SCHOOL
MATH 1

15:05.112 --> 15:06.739
Yeah, hello?

15:08.908 --> 15:10.534
Sure. What's up?

15:10.618 --> 15:13.871
Hey, what's with
the surprise food delivery?

15:13.954 --> 15:15.664
What brought this on?

15:15.748 --> 15:19.919
And Home Ec Club?
How in the world did that happen?

15:20.002 --> 15:23.088
Oh, shut up.
Besides, I haven't joined yet.

15:24.632 --> 15:26.634
Kozue and I ate it earlier.

15:27.217 --> 15:28.344
Thanks.

15:28.427 --> 15:29.345
It was good.

15:31.263 --> 15:32.306
Yeah?

15:32.389 --> 15:33.599
Good.

15:34.183 --> 15:35.476
Here, Kozue.

15:35.559 --> 15:37.561
You wanted to say something, right?

15:39.521 --> 15:41.231
It was really good,

15:41.315 --> 15:42.483
Papa.

15:42.566 --> 15:43.651
Thanks.

15:46.028 --> 15:48.739
Hey, sorry. Let me correct something.

15:48.822 --> 15:49.657
Huh?

15:49.740 --> 15:54.119
I said you should learn to wipe
your own butt, but cooking's different.

15:54.912 --> 15:57.247
The rice balls and miso soup you made...

15:57.331 --> 16:00.542
Have someone
who's important to you eat them.

16:02.127 --> 16:03.587
You see,

16:03.671 --> 16:06.382
making food for yourself is one thing,

16:06.465 --> 16:09.635
but making it for someone else
is a hundred times more fun!

16:11.303 --> 16:14.640
The miso soup was a little salty, though.

16:16.225 --> 16:17.142
Oh.

16:18.560 --> 16:19.937
Is that right?

16:20.604 --> 16:22.398
Why does your voice sound weird?

16:23.273 --> 16:24.358
Oh...

16:24.441 --> 16:25.859
I've got a cold.

16:29.321 --> 16:31.448
- Was that Eri?
- Yeah.

16:34.743 --> 16:36.203
Damn.

16:36.286 --> 16:37.997
I think I might've lost.

16:45.546 --> 16:48.132
The very next day, you joined on the spot?

16:48.215 --> 16:49.717
Talk about a fast decision!

16:49.800 --> 16:50.759
Yeah, yeah.

16:50.843 --> 16:54.013
Well, if it helps fix
some of your bad habits, then--

16:54.096 --> 16:54.972
Yeah, yeah.

16:55.055 --> 16:56.306
I said no!

16:56.974 --> 16:57.808
Aw, come on!

17:03.981 --> 17:06.025
Looks like you're as popular as ever.

17:06.108 --> 17:09.111
Oh? Wait, Mitsuoka, you, too?

17:09.194 --> 17:11.155
Huh? Me, too?

17:11.238 --> 17:13.323
Why would you be joining?

17:13.407 --> 17:15.117
Well, it's complicated.

17:15.659 --> 17:16.994
But why you, Mitsuoka?

17:17.077 --> 17:18.579
I just thought...

17:19.163 --> 17:21.623
maybe it could help out
with the ramen shop, too.

17:22.541 --> 17:25.669
But don't you dare tell anyone!

17:27.129 --> 17:30.632
And don't get too chummy with me, either!

17:30.716 --> 17:31.717
Yeah, yeah.

17:32.301 --> 17:33.886
Same as ever, huh?

17:33.969 --> 17:35.304
That's just how she is.

17:37.306 --> 17:38.766
From Eri?

17:41.268 --> 17:42.186
Huh?

17:43.937 --> 17:45.898
Boss, this is bad!

17:45.981 --> 17:47.191
What is it?

17:47.691 --> 17:49.860
We found a way for you
to get back to normal!

17:49.943 --> 17:51.111
For real?

17:51.195 --> 17:53.030
Without further ado...

17:54.573 --> 17:56.825
you need to marry Noren Mitsuoka!

17:58.994 --> 18:00.996
What the hell are you talking about?

18:01.080 --> 18:03.457
- I'm telling you--
- I heard you, that's why!

18:03.540 --> 18:08.045
What the hell are you talking about?!
How does that get me back to normal?

18:08.712 --> 18:12.925
Just now, Mitsuoka Pharmaceuticals
put out a pretty insane announcement!

18:13.008 --> 18:17.221
That Noren Mitsuoka's fiancé
will inherit the company.

18:17.304 --> 18:18.180
What?!

18:18.764 --> 18:21.934
An announcement like that
would get nothing but backlash!

18:22.017 --> 18:24.186
What they're really after is unclear.

18:24.269 --> 18:27.564
If that were all, it'd still feel
like somebody else's problem...

18:27.648 --> 18:31.193
but do you remember
what that kidnapper said?

18:31.693 --> 18:37.616
"We don't know what it is exactly,
but there's no doubt that she has it."

18:37.699 --> 18:39.076
Actually, that, too

18:39.159 --> 18:42.246
is circulating behind the scenes
as highly credible information.

18:43.038 --> 18:46.125
To sum it up, if you want to learn
the secret of that wasp,

18:46.208 --> 18:48.585
threats and brute force won't work.

18:48.669 --> 18:50.629
The only way is to inherit the company.

18:50.712 --> 18:52.005
Which means...

18:52.089 --> 18:54.800
becoming Noren Mitsuoka's fiancé.

18:54.883 --> 18:57.136
That's your new mission, Boss!

18:57.219 --> 18:58.512
As if I could do that!

18:58.595 --> 19:01.974
A divorced guy pushing 40
becoming a middle schooler's fiancé?

19:02.057 --> 19:04.768
Man, maybe I should just confess
my love to her!

19:04.852 --> 19:07.437
Not a bad idea!
If you actually got with her,

19:07.521 --> 19:09.273
you'd be the president of Mitsuoka!

19:09.356 --> 19:11.358
Being a gold digger is the dream!

19:11.441 --> 19:13.193
"Being a gold digger," nice.

19:13.277 --> 19:15.237
Yeah, I guess it would be impossible...

19:15.320 --> 19:17.990
Don't ever say that again, even as a joke.

19:18.073 --> 19:20.492
NATSUKIYA
RAMEN

19:23.036 --> 19:26.165
Ah, so good!
As long as I'm eating ramen here,

19:26.248 --> 19:28.041
I can forget all about everything!

19:28.125 --> 19:31.503
What about this fiancé stuff?
No way an old man could do that.

19:31.587 --> 19:35.215
I might be back at square one
with getting my old body back,

19:35.299 --> 19:37.050
but whatever happens, happens. Screw it!

19:40.429 --> 19:41.597
Thanks for the meal!

19:41.680 --> 19:42.639
Much appreciated!

19:43.765 --> 19:46.685
- Ogami, you never change.
- Hmm?

19:47.269 --> 19:48.270
Oh...

19:48.353 --> 19:50.105
Sounds like things are rough for you.

19:50.189 --> 19:53.692
I heard people have been coming on to you
even more than before.

19:53.775 --> 19:56.570
Well, I'm just here for the ramen, so...

19:59.448 --> 20:01.617
Noren, you can head out now.

20:02.242 --> 20:03.285
Ah, okay.

20:04.578 --> 20:06.538
This seriously sucks!

20:06.622 --> 20:09.041
Why would your dad do something like that?

20:09.124 --> 20:12.169
How should I know?
He barely ever comes home lately!

20:12.252 --> 20:15.047
And honestly,
I never want to see his face again!

20:15.756 --> 20:17.841
What the hell is his problem?

20:18.592 --> 20:20.260
Idiot!

20:20.844 --> 20:22.304
Right, Ogami?

20:22.387 --> 20:24.014
You're not even listening!

20:24.890 --> 20:27.517
Oh, yeah, that really sounds rough.

20:27.601 --> 20:30.979
Don't ask me about it
and then stop listening halfway through!

20:31.063 --> 20:32.272
No, for real...

20:32.356 --> 20:34.399
- I totally get it.
- Yeah, right!

20:34.483 --> 20:36.151
Anyway, about tomorrow's English--

20:36.235 --> 20:37.694
Already changing the subject?

20:44.743 --> 20:46.995
This is kind of nice, actually!

20:47.746 --> 20:49.122
Ah, crap!

20:49.748 --> 20:51.458
This is the kind of

20:51.541 --> 20:54.461
pointless back-and-forth
I want to have with friends.

20:56.004 --> 20:58.632
- Maybe I can do that in the club?
- Huh?

20:58.715 --> 21:00.592
Make that kind of friend!

21:00.676 --> 21:02.386
Oh, yeah.

21:03.387 --> 21:06.890
Not that I'm saying
you're that kind of friend, though.

21:07.557 --> 21:08.475
What?

22:40.067 --> 22:42.360
It's finally club time, Boss!

22:42.444 --> 22:43.528
Yeah!

22:43.612 --> 22:46.656
Gotta learn to wipe my own butt!

22:47.365 --> 22:50.077
Is that really the right energy
to bring into this?

22:50.660 --> 22:51.787
Sis...

22:51.870 --> 22:55.207
Hey, we've got a bit of a problem.

22:56.083 --> 22:57.375
What?!

22:57.459 --> 23:00.545
We've been flooded with applicants since.

23:00.629 --> 23:02.714
Most of them are here because of Noren.

23:02.798 --> 23:04.382
Joining Home Ec, too?

23:04.466 --> 23:07.010
- Wow, what a coincidence!
- Like hell it is!

23:07.094 --> 23:09.721
Actually, I've always loved home ec!

23:09.805 --> 23:12.307
"Loved home ec"?
What the hell does that even mean?

23:13.975 --> 23:16.603
Tama, could you get Hashikan for me?

23:22.943 --> 23:26.446
Shut up already!

23:27.739 --> 23:29.449
Let me make one thing clear!

23:30.033 --> 23:32.619
I already have a boyfriend!

23:34.037 --> 23:36.748
It's Juzo Ogami right here!

23:36.832 --> 23:38.750
What?!

23:38.834 --> 23:40.877
What?!
